    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the flow reads cleanly. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) are now consolidated into **one derived `identityKey`** = `normalizedTelephone + \"|\" + (email or empty) + \"|\" + (householdId or empty)`, and a create is rejected with **409** only when a new owner's *whole* key matches an existing owner's.\n\n### New units (each with a single responsibility)\n- **`util/IdentityKey`** \u2014 pure derivation of the key from an `Owner`. Reused by both the create-path check and the response mapper, so the formula lives in exactly one place.\n- **`rest/validation/IdentityDuplicateValidator`** \u2014 decides duplication by comparing whole identity keys against a set of existing owners (mirrors the style of the existing `HouseholdDuplicateValidator`).\n- **`rest/validation/DuplicateIdentityException`** \u2014 the single 409 exception (`FIELD = \"identityKey\"`), replacing the three removed ones.\n\n### Removed\n- `DuplicateTelephoneException`, `DuplicateEmailException`, `DuplicateHouseholdException` and their three handlers in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` (replaced by one handler).\n\n### Wiring\n- **Controller** `addOwner`: normalizes telephone/email, then `rejectIfDuplicateIdentity` looks up owners with the same (normalized) telephone \u2014 the only owners that *can* share the full key \u2014 and rejects on a full-key match. The former `applyHouseholdPolicy` (which used to throw on a shared household) is split into `assignHousehold` (sets `householdSize`/`householdId`, no DB writes, no rejection) and `joinHousehold` (stamps existing members' `householdId`), with the join deliberately run **after** the duplicate check so a rejected create never mutates existing owners.\n- **`OwnerMapper`** returns `identityKey` via `IdentityKey.of(owner)`, and the OpenAPI `Owner` schema gained a read-only `identityKey` field so it's exposed on both create and GET responses.\n\n### Behaviour change (as specified)\nBecause the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys and are **both allowed** \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\nCompilation and the full test suite pass (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the acceptance `coreRejectsIdentityCollision` test, which creates two owners sharing only a telephone and expects 409).",
